# UDP knock listener (idle-shutdown/knock-wake spec §4.2, §6). Longrun, NOT a
# palwarden-run-periodic timer: the listener holds bounded leases on the game
# port and must react to packets, not ticks.
#
# Runs as ROOT (no s6-setuidgid, like jobd/memory-watch): waking the server
# means starting its s6 service, which requires s6 service control, and the
# wake path takes the shared lifecycle lock the root controllers hold
# (update/restore/graceful-restart). KNOCK_ENABLED is NOT an entrypoint
# service gate — the listener decides enablement per lease and reloads the
# ops config continuously, so toggling knock from the browser needs no
# service or container restart (spec §7.2). When disabled it closes the
# socket by the next lease boundary and idles.
exec /usr/local/sbin/palworld-knock daemon
